---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Episode 3: The Trust Gap">
  <h1>Episode 3: The trust gap</h1>
  <p>
    AI can generate code faster, but speed alone does not make software safe to ship. The central
    lesson of this episode is to close the trust gap with a reliable path from review to production.
  </p>
  <div class="card">
    <strong>Keep the guardrails in the delivery path.</strong> Review AI-assisted changes, check
    dependencies and secrets, and make CI/CD enforce the checks before deployment.
  </div>
  <h2>Put it into practice</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Review each pull request for correctness and unintended changes.</li>
    <li>Keep dependencies and credentials visible to security checks.</li>
    <li>Require passing build and security gates before deploying.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    These steps address software supply-chain risk across the whole lifecycle. See the
    <a href="../secure-supply-chain/">secure supply chain lesson</a> and
    <a href="../pipeline/">delivery pipeline</a> for the details.
  </p>
</Layout>
